              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 5,
              "content_markdown": "$$m^2 - \\frac{m^4}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}$$",
              "guidance_markdown": "For correct quartic in any form.",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                8
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            },
            {
              "mark_code": "M1",
              "part_path": [
                "b"
              ],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 6,
              "content_markdown": "$$m^4 - 4m^2 + 2 = 0 \\Rightarrow m^2 = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{16-8}}{2} \\quad [= 2 \\pm \\sqrt{2}]$$",
              "guidance_markdown": "For solving their three term quartic to find $$m^2$$.",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                8
